# Excalidraw Protected Files

NEVER modify these Excalidraw core files without explicit approval:

- `packages/excalidraw/scene/Renderer.ts` — render pipeline
- `packages/excalidraw/actions/manager.tsx` — action system
- `packages/excalidraw/data/restore.ts` — file format compat
- `packages/excalidraw/types.ts` — core types

Changes to protected files require:

1. Full understanding of dependencies
2. Running complete test suite
3. Manual QA verification

## How to Verify

Before committing changes to protected files, verify that this rule is applied correctly:

### Protected Files Checklist

Expected protected files in Excalidraw core:
- [ ] `packages/excalidraw/scene/Renderer.ts` — render pipeline
- [ ] `packages/excalidraw/actions/manager.tsx` — action system
- [ ] `packages/excalidraw/data/restore.ts` — file format compat
- [ ] `packages/excalidraw/types.ts` — core types

### Code Review Checklist

- [ ] **Dependencies mapped**: Understand all files that import from the protected file
- [ ] **Tests passing**: Run `yarn test:update` to verify all tests pass
- [ ] **Type safety**: Run `yarn test:typecheck` to ensure no TypeScript errors
- [ ] **No breaking changes**: Confirm API signatures remain backward compatible
- [ ] **Documentation updated**: Update comments/docs if behavior changes

### Verification Steps

**To verify this rule is triggered for protected files:**

```bash
# 1. Check which files would trigger the rule (glob: packages/excalidraw/**)
ls -la packages/excalidraw/scene/Renderer.ts
ls -la packages/excalidraw/actions/manager.tsx
ls -la packages/excalidraw/data/restore.ts
ls -la packages/excalidraw/types.ts

# 2. Check for files that depend on the protected files
rg "from.*Renderer" packages/excalidraw --type ts --type tsx | head -10
rg "from.*manager" packages/excalidraw --type ts --type tsx | head -10
rg "from.*restore" packages/excalidraw --type ts --type tsx | head -10
rg "from.*types" packages/excalidraw --type ts --type tsx | head -10

# 3. Run complete test suite
yarn test:update

# 4. Type check
yarn test:typecheck

# 5. Build to catch compilation errors
yarn build
```

### Risk Assessment

- [ ] Change is minimal and isolated
- [ ] No changes to exported public APIs
- [ ] Core algorithm logic unchanged
- [ ] Performance impact assessed
- [ ] Backward compatibility maintained